    "statement": "A laboratory controlled study on genetically modified maize expressing Bacillus thuringiensis kurstaki (Btk) toxin reported that pollen from the genetically modified maize did not reduce survival of eastern tiger swallowtail or spicebush swallowtail caterpillars compared to pollen from non-genetically modified maize.",
